' @guidance:
' Create or update the PlantUML diagram describing how files tagged with the
' @guidance marker are processed. This is a SEPARATE way of using Ghostwriter
' and is NOT part of the Act/episode functionality.
' Keep this diagram simple: a short linear flow with one decision point,
' minimal notes, and no swimlane color-partitions.

@startuml
title Ghostwriter - @guidance Tag File Processing (standalone mode, not an Act)

skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #F5F7FA
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #4A6FA5
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF3CD
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #EDF7ED

start

:Scan project and modules for files;
note right
  Reuses standard file traversal.
end note

:Take next file;

:Pick a reviewer matching the file's extension;

if (Reviewer found and "@guidance:" marker present?) then (yes)
  :Extract guidance text;
  note right
    The marker stays unchanged in the file.
  end note
  :Build prompt from instructions,
  guidance rules, and guidance text;
  :Send prompt to AI provider;
  :Record result in report;
  note right
    getReport() here is separate from
    the Act pipeline's getResults().
  end note
else (no)
  :Skip file;
endif

note right
  Repeated for every file found
  in the scanned scope.
end note

stop

legend right
  * Standalone mode: GuidanceProcessor extends AIFileProcessor
  * Instructions live inside the file as a "@guidance:" comment
    and are never removed, so runs are repeatable.
endlegend

@enduml